      "text": "The system shall compute, on every request without ever persisting the result, whether an invoice is overdue."
     },
     {
      "n": 2,
      "text": "An invoice is overdue only if its status is in a configured list of open statuses that has no default value and must be set at deployment."
     },
     {
      "n": 3,
      "text": "An invoice with a null due date is never classified as overdue."
     },
     {
      "n": 4,
      "text": "An invoice is overdue when the number of calendar days from its due date to today, computed in a configured business time zone, is at least a configured overdue threshold that defaults to 7."
     },
     {
      "n": 5,
      "text": "When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue."
     },
     {
      "n": 6,
      "text": "Each returned overdue invoice shall include its invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, and days overdue calculated as calendar days since the due date."
     },
     {
      "n": 7,
      "text": "When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer."
     },
     {
      "n": 8,
      "text": "When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall within the named fixed bucket: 7-30, 31-60, or 61+, with limits inclusive."
     },
     {
      "n": 9,
      "text": "These bucket boundaries are fixed and are not shifted by the configured overdue threshold."
     },
     {
      "n": 10,
      "text": "If the requested bucket value is not one of the three defined buckets, the API shall respond 400 with a validation error identifying the bucket parameter."
     },
     {
      "n": 11,
      "text": "If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint lacks a valid authentication token, the API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email, or changing data."
     },
